# Reports

A report is one user's account of a scam. `App\Models\Report` stores `user_id`, `title`, `description`, and `is_active`. Products, proofs, scammers, and organizations are related records.

Public creates go through `StoreScammerReportRequest` or `StoreOrganizationReportRequest`, then `StoreScammerReportCommand` or `StoreOrganizationReportCommand`, then `ReportUsecase`. The request trims `title`, `email`, scammer and organization names, and title-cases each product name.

## Body

- `title`: required string, max 50.
- `description`: required string.
- `email`: required, `email:rfc`, max 255.
- `products`: required array, at least one item. Each item is a string, max 75.
- `profile_picture`: optional string. It is a temporary public path, not the file upload.
- `proofs`: optional array of temporary public paths.
- `contacts` and `payment_methods`: each may be omitted. At least one of the two arrays must be non-empty. When both are empty, validation fails with `A contact or a payment method is required.` on `contacts` and on `payment_methods`.
- `contacts.*.reference`: required string, max 255. `contacts.*.platform` is prohibited.
- `payment_methods.*.reference`: required string, max 255. `payment_methods.*.type` is prohibited. Typing rules are in `payment-methods.mdc`.
- Scammer report: `scammer.name` required, max 100. `organizations` optional.
- Organization report: `organization.name` required, max 100. `scammers` optional.

A linked scammer or organization does not count as the required contact or payment method. That check reads only the top-level `contacts` and `payment_methods`.

## Report against an existing record

`POST /api/public/scammers/{id}/reports` and `POST /api/public/organizations/{id}/reports` file a report against an active scammer or organization. They do not create or rename that record. A missing, inactive, or soft-deleted id is not found.

These creates go through `StoreAttachedReportRequest`, then `StoreReportForScammerCommand` or `StoreReportForOrganizationCommand`, then `ReportUsecase`. The request trims `title` and `email`, and title-cases each product name.

- `title`: required string, max 50.
- `description`: required string.
- `email`: required, `email:rfc`, max 255.
- `products`: required array, at least one item. Each item is a string, max 75.
- `proofs`: optional array of temporary public paths. The same temporary-file check and copy used by a new report applies. Scammer proofs are stored under `reports/scammers/proofs`. Organization proofs are stored under `reports/organizations/proofs`.

These bodies do not accept contacts, payment methods, or a profile picture. An invalid id is `400`.

## Images

Upload the file before the report body.

- Profile picture: `POST /api/public/media/profiles` with `StoreProfilePictureRequest`, field `image`. One file, `jpg`, `jpeg`, `png`, or `webp`, max 5120 KB. `MediaUsecase::storeTemporaryProfilePicture` stores it under `tmp/reports/profiles`.
- Proofs: `StoreProofRequest`, field `images`. At least one file, same mime types and size. `ReportUsecase::storeTemporaryProofs` stores them under `tmp/reports/proofs`.

The report body then passes those published temporary paths. `ReportUsecase` copies a profile into `reports/scammers/profiles` or `reports/organizations/profiles`, and proofs into `reports/scammers/proofs` or `reports/organizations/proofs`. A path that is not a published temporary file fails validation.
